    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'atmosphere_mass_content_of_halon1202'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Content" indicates a quantity per unit area. The "atmosphere content" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including "content_of_atmosphere_layer" are used. The mass is the total mass of the molecules. The chemical formula for Halon1202 is CBr2F2. The IUPAC name for Halon1202 is dibromo(difluoro)methane.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CF12N48'^^xsd:string .
